<title>UK: CFD sets two-tranche domestic bond for 1.5 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>CFD sets two-tranche domestic bond for 1.5 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caisse Francaise de Developpement has launched a two-tranche domestic bond for a total of 1.5 billion French francs, lead manager Caisse des Depots et Consignations said.</p>
<p>The first tranche is for 1.0 billion francs with an 11-year maturity. The deal pays Tec 10 minus 110 basis points. Reoffer is 99.68.</p>
<p>The second tranche is for 500 million francs with a 12-year maturity. The deal pays Tec 10 minus 110 basis points. Reoffer is 99.66.  </p>
<p>* * * *</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS</p>
<p> BORROWER   CAISSE FRANCAISE DE DEVELOPPEMENT</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  FRANCE (RATED AAA/AAA)</p>
<p> BASE	 TEC 10    PAY DATE    16.SEP.96</p>
<p> SPREAD     -110 BP   FULL FEES   1.30</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.55	SELL CONC   0.75</p>
<p> LISTING    PARIS     DENOMS (K)  FIVE</p>
<p> GOV LAW    FRENCH    HOME CTRY   FRANCE</p>
<p> NOTES	QUARTERLY COUPON</p>
<p>* * * *</p>
<p>TRANCE A</p>
<p> AMT    1.0 BLN FFR   MATURITY    16.SEP.07</p>
<p> ISS PRICE  100.63    REOFFER     99.68</p>
